SUMMARY:CLACS Faculty Research Symposium with Luciana Namorato
DESCRIPTION:The Center for Latin American and Caribbean Studies (CLACS) w
 elcomes Dr. Luciana Namorato for The Other Fridas: Hidden Voices\, New Hi
 stories &amp\; Future Agendas of Latin American Women Artists\, part of t
 he Fall 2026 CLACS Faculty Research Symposium.  Thursday\, November 12th|
  1-2PM | Hamilton Lugar School GA2134  This presentation explores the rec
 ognition and representation of Latin American women artists\, considering
  how their voices and experiences can expand our understanding of the reg
 ion's artistic histories.  Dr. Namorato is an associate professor in the 
 Department of Spanish and Portuguese and co-editor of The Other Fridas: T
 he Lives and Works of Latin American Women Artists. Her research includes
  Brazilian and Portuguese literature\, gender studies\, and contemporary 
 Latin American literature.
