LOCATION:Lilly Library (1200 E. Seventh St.)
GEO:39.167909;-86.518974
SUMMARY:Guided tours of the Lilly Library
DESCRIPTION:You'll visit the Lilly's main galleries\, and your expert gui
 de will talk about some of the Lilly's highlights including the Gutenberg
  Bible&#160\;and our current exhibitions from the Lilly Library collectio
 ns: The Declaration of Independence: The Motives\, the Moment (https://li
 braries.indiana.edu/lilly-library/declaration-independence) and The Signe
 rs (https://libraries.indiana.edu/lilly-library/the-signers). Additional 
 hands-on time with rotating selections from the collections will follow. 
 These selections include medieval manuscripts\, artists books\, and one o
 f the John Ford's Best Director Oscars. Non-flash photography is permitte
 d\, seating is available throughout the tour\, and the building is wheelc
 hair accessible. The tour generally lasts a little less than one hour and
  is open to all.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  You'll visit the Lilly's main galleries
 \, and your expert guide will talk about some of the Lilly's highlights i
 ncluding the Gutenberg Bible&#160\;and our current exhibitions from the L
 illy Library collections: <em><a href="https://libraries.indiana.edu/lill
 y-library/declaration-independence" target="_blank" rel="noopener">The De
 claration of Independence: The Motives\, the Moment</a></em> and <em><a h
 ref="https://libraries.indiana.edu/lilly-library/the-signers" target="_bl
 ank" rel="noopener">The Signers</a></em>. Additional hands-on time with r
 otating selections from the collections will follow. These selections inc
 lude medieval manuscripts\, artists books\, and one of the John Ford's Be
 st Director Oscars. Non-flash photography is permitted\, seating is avail
 able throughout the tour\, and the building is wheelchair accessible. The
  tour generally lasts a little less than one hour and is open to all.</p>
