 0nzw1h1" data-markjs="true" data-ogac="" data-ogab="" data-ogsc="" data-o
 gsb="" data-ogsbtc="" data-ogsbrc="" data-ogsbbc="" data-ogsblc="">writin
 g</span> through close looking and conversation. Together\, we'll explore
  the observations and questions sparked by this painting\, then allow ind
 ividual time for reflective <span class="markc70nzw1h1" data-markjs="true
 " data-ogac="" data-ogab="" data-ogsc="" data-ogsb="" data-ogsbtc="" data
 -ogsbrc="" data-ogsbbc="" data-ogsblc="">writing</span> to each bring our
  own perspective.&#160\;</p><p>  Whether you're a writer or simply curiou
 s to try something new\, you'll find inspiration here and a welcoming com
 munity to share the journey.</p><h3>  What to Bring</h3><ul><li>your favo
 rite pencil (no pens).  </li><li>a notebook or paper. Clipboards are avai
 lable to borrow.  </li><li>a phone or camera to take a picture of the art
  for later reference.  </li></ul><p>  &#160\;</p><h3><strong><span data-c
