DTSTART:20261209T163000Z
DTEND:20261209T170000Z
LOCATION:SIDNEY AND LOIS ESKENAZI MUSEUM OF ART
SUMMARY:Curator-led Tour
DESCRIPTION:IU Contemporary Dance students have selected artworks in the 
 exhibition as inspiration for an interpretative dance performance at noon
 . They will perform original choreography\, inspired by the exhibition.  
 Before the dance performance\, join Ben Levy\, Glaubinger Curator of Work
 s on Paper\, for a guided short tour to learn more about some of the phot
 ographs that inspired the dance performance.&#160\; &#160\;Read more abou
 t this exhibition. (https://artmuseum.indiana.edu/exhibitions/2026-08-29-
 photographic-reflex-marks-deprez.html)  &#160\;Know Before You GoNo need 
 to RSVP for this instance.  Meet us at Featured Exhibitions Gallery on th
 e first floor of the Eskenazi Museum.&#160\;  A small handbag may be carr
 ied at your side. Larger bags and backpacks will need to be stored before
  touring. Free lockers are available.&#160\;We recommend arriving a few m
 inutes early to store belongings.Admission and tours are free.Read about 
 where to find us\, where to park\, accessibility\, and museum guidelines.
 When You ArriveFor help finding the gallery\, check in with Guest Service
 s staff at the welcome desk on the first floor.If you park in the IMU par
 king lot\, Guest Services can validate your parking voucher for a discoun
 t.Store backpacks and large bags before touring. Lockers and coat racks a
 re available on the first floor\, past the welcome desk.Keep space (18") 
 between yourself\, including anything you're carrying\, and the art.
